 "final_summary": "The bug was caused by a race condition in the `next()` method of `TicketSequence`, where the value of `self._next` was read before acquiring the lock. The fix ensures atomicity by acquiring the lock before reading and incrementing the value, guaranteeing unique ticket numbers under concurrent requests. The read and increment operation is now fully protected within the lock, preventing any race conditions.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/sequence.py b/tracker/sequence.py\nindex aa19a59..90b37b2 100644\n--- a/tracker/sequence.py\n+++ b/tracker/sequence.py\n@@ -13,8 +13,8 @@ class TicketSequence:\n         self._next = value\n \n     def next(self):\n-        current = self._next\n         with self._lock:\n+            current = self._next\n             self._store(current + 1)\n         self.issued.append(current)\n         return current\n",
